      "DetectedLanguage": "en",
      "AnswerText": "Set the NavMeshAgent.autoTraverseOffMeshLink property to false to prevent automatic traversal of an OffMeshLink. When this is disabled, the agent will pause on the link, and you can then use the NavMeshAgent.CompleteOffMeshLink() method to manually complete the movement. This allows for custom movement control over the link.",
      "CitationUrls": [
        "https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.3/Documentation/ScriptReference/AI.NavMeshAgent-autoTraverseOffMeshLink.html",
        "https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.3/Documentation/ScriptReference/AI.NavMeshAgent-isOnOffMeshLink.html",
        "https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.3/Documentation/ScriptReference/AI.NavMeshAgent.CompleteOffMeshLink.html"
      ],
      "ExpectedSourceUrls": [
        "https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.3/Documentation/ScriptReference/AI.NavMeshAgent-autoTraverseOffMeshLink.html"
      ],
      "ExpectedFacts": [
        "autoTraverseOffMeshLink controls whether the agent traverses OffMeshLinks automatically.",
        "Setting it to false allows special control over that movement."
      ]
    },
