      "StatusMatches": true,
      "ExpectedLanguage": "en",
      "DetectedLanguage": "en",
      "AnswerText": "You can read an agent\u0027s current traversal cost for a NavMesh area using the NavMeshAgent.GetAreaCost method, which returns a float representing the current cost for the specified area index. However, this cost applies only to pathfinding calculations and does not automatically change the agent\u0027s movement speed. The path cost reflects difficulty or environmental factors like terrain type, but it does not directly affect the agent\u0027s real-time movement speed.",
      "CitationUrls": [
        "https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.3/Documentation/ScriptReference/AI.NavMeshAgent.GetAreaCost.html",
        "https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.3/Documentation/ScriptReference/AI.NavMeshAgent.GetAreaCost.html"
      ],
      "ExpectedSourceUrls": [
        "https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.3/Documentation/ScriptReference/AI.NavMeshAgent.GetAreaCost.html"
      ],
      "ExpectedFacts": [
        "GetAreaCost(int areaIndex) returns the current cost for the specified NavMesh area index.",
        "The cost applies to pathfinding and does not automatically affect movement speed while following the path."
      ]
